 "text": "Hello, how are things going? It' a bit more than that. Most people aim for about two hundred miles, including some easy stops. At a reasonable pace, around three or four hours of riding plus stops for food and toilet breaks. It is. Plan for the out and back to take little longer than the hundred miles, just in case you run into traffic. The metro is a great way build up distance without the pressure of a whole day. Five miles at time is a lot easier at that distance. Build up gradually, maybe three or four times week, with one longer ride each month. Rest days are just as important as the active ones.",
